638	///
639	/// Per `docs/type-checker-integration.md`: the checker decides which props exist, their types, whether they are
640	/// required, `parent`, `declarations` and the component's `composes`; a description and tags come from the checker,
641	/// else the structural pass; a default value and a union's member order come from oxc's syntax, else the structural
642	/// pass ([`merge_semantic_props`]). Inheritance layers, curated inherited props and `discriminantProp` stay structural.
643	/// Components the checker did not answer for keep their structural result untouched. A structural diagnostic stops
644	/// naming a component the checker answered for when the answer supersedes it
645	/// ([`DiagnosticCode::superseded_by_checker`]), and goes once it names none.
646	///
